 calls a reproducible flake is fixed at its mechanism [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]rather than one-at-a-time as it surfaces, and a committed baseline [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]gate fails the build when a new flake node appears — so sase-ct can[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]close on a measured, enforced criterion instead of on \"the node [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]named in the latest reopen is fixed\".[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]9[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]parallel_suite_flake_class.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/parallel_suite_flake_class.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-h8[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-h8/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A contention harness for the default (non-visual) lane[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]harness[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]harness: add a `just test-contention` recipe and `run_pytest` mode that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]oversubscribes a pinned CPU set the way `test-visual-contention` already[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]does for the PNG lane, plus a repeat/soak knob and a per-node failure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tally, so the class can be reproduced and a fix can be falsified on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]demand.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One bounded-wait primitive for raw-pilot tests[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]waits[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]waits: publish a single supported bounded-wait helper for tests that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]drive a raw Textual pilot instead of `AcePage`, retire the four ad-hoc [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`_wait_until` copies onto it, and document when a bare `pause()` is and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]is not sufficient.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Measured classification of every flake node[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]triage[dim] · [dim][/dim]after harness[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]triage: run the contention harness to produce an empirical failure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]corpus, reconcile it against the durable health store's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reproducible-flake set, and commit a triage table that assigns every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]node a mechanism family and a named fix shape, so the remediation phases[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]work from measurement rather than from the bead's anecdotes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the off-pump settle-gap family[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pump[dim] · [dim][/dim]after triage, waits[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pump: fix every triaged node whose failure is a single `pause()` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]standing in for work that runs off the Textual message pump, by waiting [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on the observable end state with the shared bounded-wait primitive.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the real-wall-clock-threshold family[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]clock[dim] · [dim][/dim]after triage, waits[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]clock: remove the dependence on real elapsed wall-clock time from the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stall watchdog tests and the other triaged deadline-shaped nodes, by [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]driving them from an injectable time source or a load-normalized budget [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of loosening assertions again.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the ACE fixture-state and cross-test-leakage family[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]fixture[dim] · [dim][/dim]after triage, waits[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]fixture: fix the triaged ACE nodes whose injected fixture state is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]overwritten by a queued repaint or leaks across tests, by making state [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]injection settle-verified and the affected panes isolated per test.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the non-ACE store, tooling, and subprocess family[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tooling[dim] · [dim][/dim]after triage, waits[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tooling: fix the triaged non-ACE nodes — bead-store clusters, selection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and run_pytest tooling tests, the coverage-context cache, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]subprocess/pipe races — while leaving the bead-mutation lock timeout [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tracked separately under sase-e2 alone.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A committed flake baseline that fails the build on new flakes[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pump, clock, fixture, tooling[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate: commit a flake baseline file and a gate that fails when the health[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]store's reproducible-flake set exceeds it, wire the gate into the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exhaustive lane and a CI contention job, and add the lint check that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stops the retired ad-hoc wait helpers from coming back.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Land the epic and close sase-ct on a measured criterion[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]land[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]land: run the exit criterion on the combined tree, file any residue with[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]/sase_new_task, and close sase-ct with a note that states the root cause[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]of the class and the enforced criterion that replaces hand-adjudication.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-h8","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-h8.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-b789203ff81791d9ebac4280d979b3a0","started_at":"2026-08-07T22:09:26.735951+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"f0b79d02a925decb3cf3cf7928490d7936ad7d4f3f8f6ea8c4b4bb71443aaa57","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h8.7/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"c34620ad7b1b78f5aa22fd1cacd0270384cf3e3d570d7349bde4617b8ffd46e0","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h8.7/meta.json","size_bytes":599},"prompt":{"digest":"88aad5a32ef13c429d68c01dce2b3a24cdf9565372b8bdcad77dc6eb182f820d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h8.7/prompt.md","size_bytes":183},"state":{"digest":"c331f700efadd69c3d4d222fac3bb429e14b79fda6a78b37d03513f7e5252a9a","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-h8.7/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-h8.7","local_name":"sase-h8.7","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-h8","agent_clan_generation":"20260807180913","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-h8.7","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-h8","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-h8.7","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-d9c72d9db229d62cc974c5c060e2a4ad","started_at":"20260807180919","state":"waiting"},{"commits